{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890218",
      "title": "Form Submissions In TypeScript Projects",
      "sourceHash": "eba05c6a52afb8ac5b476bccd42aaaaf642474f31f212abd9e2482bb2920a44a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.75,
          "en": "Now that we built a lot of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.75,
          "end": 7.68,
          "en": "that dealt with outputting Todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.68,
          "end": 9.76,
          "en": "let's make sure our actual Todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.76,
          "end": 13.57,
          "en": "no longer have to be hard-coded, dummy Todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.57,
          "end": 17.153,
          "en": "but that we instead let the user enter new Todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.21,
          "end": 20.5,
          "en": "And for this I'll add yet another component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.5,
          "end": 22.54,
          "en": "the NewTodo component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.54,
          "end": 26.59,
          "en": "which should display a form that handles user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.59,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "where we get the, well, Todo as a user add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 33.88,
          "en": "For this header, I'll again, create a functional component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.88,
          "end": 37.65,
          "en": "by using const and then the arrow function syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.65,
          "end": 42.28,
          "en": "And I'll export this NewTodo component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.28,
          "end": 44.68,
          "en": "NewTodo like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.68,
          "end": 48.14,
          "en": "And here, I now wanna return my form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.14,
          "end": 50.02,
          "en": "I wanna render a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.02,
          "end": 52.77,
          "en": "that allows the user to enter a NewTodo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.27,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "Now this will be a very simple form, which I build here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 61.7,
          "en": "I wanna have a label, where I say Todo text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.7,
          "end": 63.91,
          "en": "Below that I input of type text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.91,
          "end": 66.513,
          "en": "where the user should enter the concrete Todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.67,
          "end": 70.35,
          "en": "And below that a button for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 73.5,
          "en": "adding that Todo for submitting that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.5,
          "end": 76.46000000000001,
          "en": "That's the JSX code I want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.46000000000001,
          "end": 79.24,
          "en": "We can refine the styling a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.24,
          "end": 81.41,
          "en": "For the moment, let's just add it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.41,
          "end": 84.663,
          "en": "And let's focus just on React and TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.85,
          "end": 88.283,
          "en": "Now on that label I'll add the htmlFor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.25,
          "end": 92.09,
          "en": "attribute so to say, this prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.09,
          "end": 93.49000000000001,
          "en": "to point at the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.43,
          "end": 95.593,
          "en": "text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.593,
          "end": 98.45,
          "en": "input which is this one here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.45,
          "end": 101.93,
          "en": "So I added id text here to connect the label to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.93,
          "end": 104.75,
          "en": "for accessibility. But now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.75,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "that's the finished JSX code. And what I wanna do now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 111.24000000000001,
          "en": "is I wanna handle the form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.24000000000001,
          "end": 113.87,
          "en": "and prevent the browser default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.87,
          "end": 116.03,
          "en": "as we learned it in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.03,
          "end": 121.03,
          "en": "And in addition, I wanna of course then get the user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.12,
          "end": 122.9,
          "en": "And for getting the user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.9,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "we of course learned about two main approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 131.63,
          "en": "We can either listen to every keystroke with useState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.63,
          "end": 135.55,
          "en": "or we use a Ref to then get the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.55,
          "end": 137.62,
          "en": "once the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.62,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "And it depends on what you wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "If you wanna validate with every keystroke or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 145.17000000000002,
          "en": "which approach you wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.17000000000002,
          "end": 147.62,
          "en": "And here I'll go for the Ref approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.62,
          "end": 152.62,
          "en": "because we're going to see useState in action later anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.29,
          "end": 156.73,
          "en": "Now let's start with the form submission function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.73,
          "end": 158.69,
          "en": "For this, I'll add a new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.69,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "in this component function. And that will be the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.006,
          "end": 166.203,
          "en": "submitHandler function, though the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.36,
          "end": 170.81,
          "en": "In there, I expect an event argument so that I can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.81,
          "end": 174.64,
          "en": "event.prevent default. But we can already see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.64,
          "end": 176.89,
          "en": "that I'm not getting any auto completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.89,
          "end": 180.02,
          "en": "and that we got the red squiggly lines here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.02,
          "end": 183.78,
          "en": "Now we're getting red squiggly lines, because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "TypeScript has no idea which type of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 189,
          "en": "this event thing will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189,
          "end": 190.55,
          "en": "We as a developer know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.55,
          "end": 193.67,
          "en": "that it will actually be such an event object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.67,
          "end": 197.28,
          "en": "which is emitted and passed automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.28,
          "end": 199.21,
          "en": "when we connect this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.21,
          "end": 201.64,
          "en": "to the appropriate event listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.64,
          "end": 204.653,
          "en": "But that's not something TypeScript can know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.67000000000002,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "So we have to add a type annotation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 213.45,
          "en": "And here, since we'll add this function to the submit event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.45,
          "end": 218.349,
          "en": "through React. So with help of React. With help of React's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.349,
          "end": 221.81,
          "en": "onSubmit property later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.81,
          "end": 224.45,
          "en": "Since we'll do that, the type here will be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.45,
          "end": 225.543,
          "en": "the React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.942,
          "end": 227.775,
          "en": "formEvent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 228.79,
          "end": 231.78300000000002,
          "en": "And you can actually omit this import as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.72,
          "end": 233.93,
          "en": "That's a special type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.93,
          "end": 236.51,
          "en": "provided by our React package in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.51,
          "end": 240.69,
          "en": "which is this event object type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 240.69,
          "end": 242.21,
          "en": "which we'll get automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.21,
          "end": 244.163,
          "en": "when listening to the form submission.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.03,
          "end": 247.29,
          "en": "There also is a MouseEvent, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.29,
          "end": 250.6,
          "en": "which you would get if you add onClick listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.6,
          "end": 252.7,
          "en": "That's then the event object you get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.7,
          "end": 255.87,
          "en": "But for the form submission, it's the FormEvent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.87,
          "end": 259.1,
          "en": "And then here we can call preventDefault.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.1,
          "end": 262.16,
          "en": "You now see I get all the completion, because now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 262.16,
          "end": 265.573,
          "en": "I'm clearly describing which type of data we'll get here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.81,
          "end": 269.37,
          "en": "Now we can connect this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.37,
          "end": 272.483,
          "en": "and pass the submitHandler to onSubmit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.5,
          "end": 276.15,
          "en": "By the way, if I would be using MouseEvent here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.15,
          "end": 279.22,
          "en": "you see I'm now getting an error down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.22,
          "end": 282.7,
          "en": "with a very long message basically telling me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.7,
          "end": 286.63,
          "en": "that the type of function I'm pointing at it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 286.63,
          "end": 291.2,
          "en": "for onSubmit is not the type of function React is expecting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.2,
          "end": 293.64,
          "en": "Because for the onSubmit prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.64,
          "end": 297.38,
          "en": "React is expecting a pointer and a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.38,
          "end": 300.15,
          "en": "that actually gets the argument of type FormEvent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.15,
          "end": 302.38,
          "en": "not of type MouseEvent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.38,
          "end": 305.19,
          "en": "So that's an extra little check, which we get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 305.19,
          "end": 306.6,
          "en": "which is great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.6,
          "end": 309.5,
          "en": "And now with that turn back to FormEvent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.5,
          "end": 310.943,
          "en": "everything is working again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 313.28,
          "end": 316.45,
          "en": "Now we wanna extract the entered input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 316.45,
          "end": 319.203,
          "en": "And we'll do that with help of Refs here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}